# cuts/v1.0.36/cut.env
# ============================================================================
# THE PINS FOR v1.0.36. Read by bin/rollforward_gate.sh --cut v1.0.36 and by
# scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh.
#
# WHY v1.0.36 EXISTS: NO DMG EVER CUT HAS FINISHED AN INSTALL.
#
# Andy installed v1.0.35 on a wiped 16 GB Mini. Fourteen steps green, then a
# hard abort at step 15 of 39:
#
#     install.sh:13480  _install_enrichment_agent      CALLED, at top level
#     install.sh:18386  _install_enrichment_agent() {  DEFINED, 4,906 lines later
#     -> _install_enrichment_agent: command not found
#     -> ERR-99-INSTALL-ABORT-L13549
#
# Bash creates a function when its definition line EXECUTES. The call sits in
# the main flow, so it ran 4,906 lines before the definition existed. This is
# deterministic on every box and the same line numbers were on origin/main, so
# EVERY DMG this project has ever produced carried it. v1.0.36 is the first
# build that can finish an install at all.
#
# Introduced by bdd1707 (#747) / 781bc93 (#816), "enrichment had NO invoker".
# The diagnosis was right and the invoker was placed where it cannot resolve --
# the same class as the v1.0.34 upload defect: a correct fix positioned so that
# running it breaks the run.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THE LEAK FIX SHIPS IN THE SAME CUT, AND IS NOT SEPARABLE
#
# #410 is not a passenger. Today the missing function is the only thing
# LIMITING a data leak: enrichment ran ONCE, inline, for 83 seconds, and 8
# LinkedIn InMail subjects went out to Wikidata and MusicBrainz. The agent
# #409 installs runs every 30 minutes with a 600-second budget, indefinitely.
#
# So shipping #409 ALONE does not restore the status quo. It converts a
# one-off leak into a permanent, unattended, half-hourly export of a
# customer's correspondents and their employers. #409 without #410 is a
# WORSE artefact than the broken one it replaces. They ship together or not
# at all, and they are one commit so that this is structural rather than
# something a reviewer has to remember.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE APPCAST STEP IS STILL EXPECTED TO END RED, AND THAT IS STILL THE DESIGN
#
# Unchanged from v1.0.35. OSTLER_SPARKLE_SIGNING_KEY is not among this repo's
# Actions secrets, so the hard-require fires, the step fails, and the job goes
# red WITH the DMG already uploaded, because #828 moved the upload in front of
# it (`if: always()` on staging/verify AND on upload-artifact). A red run that
# hands back a complete artefact is what #828 was built to produce.
#
# DO NOT RE-TAG ON THAT RED. Read WHICH step failed first. v1.0.34 died on the
# same colour with a different cause -- the artefact never left the runner --
# and telling those two apart is the whole job. The appcast remains a known
# dark surface tracked at #370 until Andy answers the signing-key question.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PINS BELOW ARE MEASURED, NOT ASSERTED
#
# Daemon, unchanged from v1.0.33/34/35. This cut rebuilds no daemon. Verified
# by dereferencing the ANNOTATED tag myself rather than copying the previous
# record forward:
#
#     git/ref/tags/hub-v0.4.58  -> type=tag  sha=87cd9d9e4634...
#     git/tags/87cd9d9e         -> type=commit  sha=5b7efb00a54131bf...
#
#     gui/Makefile   DAEMON_VERSION 0.4.58  DAEMON_SHA256 d4f274cb...
#     install.sh     OSTLER_ASSISTANT_VERSION 0.4.58
#     install.sh     DEFAULT_ASSISTANT_TARBALL_SHA256 d4f274cb...
#
# Wiki images v0.1.18 from CM044 bf5dfe68, unchanged from v1.0.35 and still
# bound in scripts/wiki_image_provenance.tsv:
#
#     wiki-site      sha256:635e3ee7...  bf5dfe68ad67c0707b802d76cb7658736e8c4282
#     wiki-compiler  sha256:c6a207fc...  bf5dfe68ad67c0707b802d76cb7658736e8c4282
#
# Measured, because a re-pin is TWO edits and the gate that catches the missing
# provenance row runs at CUT time, not on the PR: install.sh carries ZERO
# orphan `MediaType:`/`Digest:` tail lines and ZERO malformed pins (G1/G4).
#
# CM051 names origin/main AFTER the last merge, which is the only moment this
# pin can honestly be chosen. It was re-pointed once during preparation: the
# cut-readiness dry run went RED on check-orphans with CM051 #836 open, and
# #836 is the TNM re-review of the very leak fix this cut ships, so it was
# merged rather than deferred and the pin moved with it.
#
# Neither the version-bump branch nor #836 touches install.sh (measured: 0
# install.sh paths in either diff), so the pin and the shipping tree agree by
# CONTENT and not merely by ordering:
#
#     CM051 pin b5aa8dd1  install.sh blob  59f75bf33141b6933ff5af9726f82c13d9574786
#     origin/main         install.sh blob  59f75bf33141b6933ff5af9726f82c13d9574786
#
# RE-VERIFY IMMEDIATELY BEFORE PUSHING THE TAG, AFTER THE LAST MERGE, NOT
# BEFORE IT:
#
#     git rev-parse $CM051:install.sh
#     git rev-parse origin/main:install.sh
#
# If they diverge, re-point CM051 to main and re-run. A pin chosen early and
# trusted is what burnt v1.0.31.
# ============================================================================

# The daemon. hub-v0.4.58, signed, notarised and stapled. Unchanged from
# v1.0.33, v1.0.34 and v1.0.35 -- this cut rebuilds no daemon. DEREFERENCED
# commit: the tag is ANNOTATED and its tag object is 87cd9d9e, and recording
# that would pin the cut to a tag object rather than to source.
DAEMON_COMMIT=5b7efb00a541

# The CM051 tree whose install.sh ships in the DMG. See the blob note above.
CM051=b5aa8dd10c507d897da095646aa39d842ec3869b
